Sorry, I’ve just realized I’m talking nonsense, and wasting people’s time. Just in case I’ve have sown unnecessary confusion:

Overall Probability of detection given by number of animals seen, divided by the estimated nos present.

> length(ddf.result$fitted)/sum(1/ddf.result$fitted)

[1] 0.4890873

The same answer as given by mrds

summary(ddf.result)$average.p

[1] 0.4890873

And not the same answer as is obtained by taking a simple mean of the fitted values.

> mean(ddf.result$fitted)

[1] 0.5348632

To get probability of detection for individuals rather than objects:

sum(ddf.result$data$size)/sum(ddf.result$data$size/ddf.result$fitted)

[1] 0.6286722

